# Shinobi attribution and third-party notices

## Project provenance

Shinobi is a modified fork of an earlier free-software YouTube client (version 0.5.20) written
by Decio Crytek and released under the GNU GPL version 3, taken from commit
`58d69b4f96563afc2d071c1ac31b3777831ca221`. The original author's attribution and the GPL
license are preserved; only the fork's own name and visual identity are new. This derivative
has been reorganized and extended with a Shinobi theme, on-device signed-out history, caption
selection/parsing, SponsorBlock ad skipping, tests and project documentation. The upstream GPL
text is included as `LICENSE`.

## Bundled or referenced open-source projects

- [NewPipeExtractor](https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor) — GPL-3.0. Used for
  YouTube extraction and data parsing.
- [AndroidX](https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx), [Jetpack Compose](https://developer.android.com/jetpack/compose),
  and [AndroidX Media3](https://github.com/androidx/media) — Apache-2.0.
- [OkHttp](https://github.com/square/okhttp) — Apache-2.0 and MIT (dual-licensed).
- [Coil](https://github.com/coil-kt/coil) — Apache-2.0.
- [Guava](https://github.com/google/guava) — Apache-2.0.
- [Gradle Wrapper](https://github.com/gradle/gradle) — Apache-2.0; the wrapper JAR and launcher scripts are included.
- [SponsorBlock](https://sponsor.ajay.app) — community segment data and service, attributed in-app;
  data is identified there as CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

The links above point to each project's license and attribution materials. No paid APIs,
proprietary SDKs, or ad/analytics SDKs are included.
